From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <daniel@matv.io>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] af: settle the lens before scoring, real fine pass, cover
 the macro end

Field symptom (post focus-loss-debounce deploy): focus locks and holds,
but the LOCKED POSITION is often wrong for near/macro subjects -- close
text and objects render soft while far scenes look fine.

Mechanism -- three compounding sweep defects:

 1. Lag-contaminated scoring. The sweep scored ONE frame per position
    back-to-back, but a sharpness sample delivered with frame N was
    exposed 1-2 frame times before the lens command issued at frame N-1
    landed (in-flight buffers; libcamera's default sensor exposureDelay
    is 2), and the lc898217xc VCM itself needs ~80 ms to settle
    (measured on fajita) -- 1-2 frame times at the soft ISP's real
    10-20 fps. Each sample was therefore attributed to a position 1-2
    steps AHEAD of the one that exposed it, dragging the recorded peak
    2-4 knob units (~40-80 of 2047 DAC counts) past the true peak in
    the sweep direction. Far subjects hide that inside their generous
    depth of field; near subjects, whose sharpness-vs-position curve is
    steepest, do not.

 2. Dead refinement pass. After the coarse pass `step /= 10` turned
    step 2 into 0.2 and the `if (step > 0.2)` guard was false, so the
    fine pass never ran: the lock came straight from the coarse pass's
    contaminated argmax. (The sharpness_max reset for a second pass was
    unreachable code.)

 3. Macro end never sampled. The loop scored a position, incremented,
    and continued only `while (pos < stop)` -- with step 2 the scored
    positions were 0,2,...,98 and position 100 (VCM DAC 2047, the macro
    end: DAC 0 = spring rest = infinity) was never evaluated, clipping
    exactly the close-focus extreme the field complaint is about.

Fix:

 - Per-position settling: after every lens move, discard kSettleFrames
   (3: 2-frame command-to-exposure pipeline depth + 1 frame budgeted
   for the per-step VCM settle) frames and score the next one, so each
   sample was exposed entirely at its recorded position
   (kBigMoveSettleFrames = 5 for the large pass-start/lock jumps,
   whose ~80 ms-or-worse settle gets 3 budgeted frames). This removes
   the systematic bias at its source rather than guessing an exact lag
   to re-pair samples with earlier commands (queue depth varies with
   load and fps).
 - Real two-pass sweep: coarse 0..100 step 5 (21 samples, macro end
   included), then a fine pass over the coarse peak +-5 at step 1.
 - Parabolic interpolation over the fine maximum and its two settled
   neighbours refines the lock below fine-step granularity (~+-10 DAC
   counts), clamped to half a step against noise.
 - The focus-loss baseline is seeded from the first SETTLED frame at
   the final lock position instead of the sweep maximum (largest of ~30
   noisy samples, biased high and possibly AGC-drifted). The debounce
   logic itself is unchanged.
 - updateFocus() now adds focus_min into the knob->DAC mapping (no-op
   on fajita where focus_min = 0, correct where it isn't).

Frame budget at the soft ISP's 10-20 fps:
  coarse: 5 settle + 21 scored + 20x3 settle = 86 frames
  fine:   5 settle + 11 scored + 10x3 settle = 46 frames
  lock:   5 settle + 1 baseline seed         =  6 frames
  total ~138 frames = 6.9 s @ 20 fps, 13.8 s @ 10 fps
  (before: ~70 frames = 3.5-7 s, but ~50 of those scored samples were
  attributed to the wrong lens position; the extra seconds buy a lock
  that is correct for the thin near-field depth of field. If sweep
  time ever matters more, kSettleFrames = 2 brings the total back to
  ~108 frames = 5.4-10.8 s at the cost of scoring the per-step frame
  right at the settle deadline -- see the derivation at the constant.)
---

diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
index 3db6dcb..7f81af5 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,78 @@ static constexpr uint64_t kFocusLostDen = 100;
 static constexpr unsigned int kBaselineRiseShift = 3;
 static constexpr unsigned int kBaselineDecayShift = 6;
 
+/*
+ * CDAF sweep tuning.
+ *
+ * LensPosition knob units are 0..100 across the VCM's whole
+ * V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE range (updateFocus() maps linearly), so one
+ * unit is 1% of mechanical travel -- ~20 DAC counts on fajita's
+ * lc898217xc (0..2047, DAC 0 = spring rest = infinity end, 2047 =
+ * macro end).
+ *
+ * Sharpness samples are late relative to lens commands: the command
+ * issued when frame N's stats complete only affects frames exposed 1-2
+ * frame times later (in-flight buffers; libcamera's default sensor
+ * exposureDelay is 2 frames), and the VCM itself needs ~80 ms to
+ * mechanically settle (measured on fajita's lc898217xc) -- 1-2 frame
+ * times at the soft ISP's real-world 10-20 fps. Scoring one frame per
+ * position back-to-back therefore attributes each sample to a lens
+ * position 1-2 sweep steps ahead of the one that exposed it, dragging
+ * the recorded peak past the true peak in the sweep direction. The
+ * error is worst where the sharpness curve is steepest -- near/macro
+ * subjects, whose depth of field is thinnest.
+ */
+
+/*
+ * Frames discarded after every per-step lens move before one frame is
+ * scored, so the scored frame was exposed entirely at the commanded
+ * position. Derivation: command-to-exposure pipeline depth (2 frames,
+ * libcamera's default sensor exposureDelay) + ceil(settle / frame
+ * time). The ~80 ms settle was measured for LARGE jumps; per-step
+ * moves (1-5 knob units, ~20-102 DAC counts) settle faster but are
+ * unmeasured, so budget 1 frame at the soft ISP's 10-20 fps
+ * (50-100 ms frames): 2 + 1 = 3. With only 2 discarded frames the
+ * scored frame at 20 fps can be exposed ~50 ms after the move, while
+ * the lens may still be settling -- exactly the misattribution this
+ * patch removes. If small-step settle is ever measured under one
+ * frame time, kSettleFrames = 2 is the faster knob (~30 fewer frames
+ * per sweep).
+ */
+static constexpr uint32_t kSettleFrames = 3;
+
+/*
+ * Settle for large jumps (sweep start, pass transition, final move to
+ * the lock position): these can cross the whole 0..2047 DAC range.
+ * Same derivation: 2 pipeline frames + ceil(settle / frame time). The
+ * ~80 ms measurement is already 2 frames at 20 fps with zero margin,
+ * and a full-range jump can settle slower than what was measured, so
+ * budget 3 frames: 2 + 3 = 5.
+ */
+static constexpr uint32_t kBigMoveSettleFrames = 5;
+
+/*
+ * Coarse pass step in knob units (~102 DAC counts): positions
+ * 0,5,...,100 = 21 samples, so the macro end (100) is sampled exactly
+ * (the old loop's exclusive bound never scored it). The coarse pass
+ * only needs to bracket the peak within one step for the fine pass;
+ * don't go much coarser or a thin near-subject sharpness lobe can fall
+ * between samples.
+ */
+static constexpr double kCoarseStep = 5.0;
+
+/*
+ * Fine pass: +-kFineSpan window around the coarse peak, stepped by
+ * kFineStep (~20 DAC counts). With settled scoring the true peak lies
+ * within one coarse step of the coarse maximum, so the span is one
+ * coarse step. The lock position is then refined below fine-step
+ * granularity by parabolic interpolation.
+ */
+static constexpr double kFineStep = 1.0;
+static constexpr double kFineSpan = kCoarseStep;
+
+/* Tolerance for accumulated floating-point error in position stepping. */
+static constexpr double kPosEpsilon = 1e-6;
+
 namespace ipa::soft::algorithms {
 
 Af::Af()
@@ -119,7 +191,12 @@ void Af::queueRequest([[maybe_unused]] typename Module::Context &context,
 
 void Af::updateFocus([[maybe_unused]] IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] IPAFrameContext &frameContext, [[maybe_unused]] double exposureMSV)
 {
-	frameContext.lens.focus_pos = context.activeState.knobs.focus_pos.value_or(50.0) / 100.0 * (context.configuration.focus.focus_max - context.configuration.focus.focus_min);
+	/*
+	 * Map knob units (0..100) onto the whole V4L2 focus range,
+	 * offset by focus_min (0 on fajita's lc898217xc, where 100 ==
+	 * DAC 2047 == the macro end, but nonzero minima exist).
+	 */
+	frameContext.lens.focus_pos = context.configuration.focus.focus_min + context.activeState.knobs.focus_pos.value_or(50.0) / 100.0 * (context.configuration.focus.focus_max - context.configuration.focus.focus_min);
 }
 
 static int steps;
@@ -130,8 +207,20 @@ void Af::restart(IPAContext &context) {
 	context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max = 0;
 	context.configuration.focus.start = 0;
 	context.configuration.focus.stop = 100;
-	context.configuration.focus.step = 2;
-	context.configuration.focus.skip = 10;
+	context.configuration.focus.step = kCoarseStep;
+	/*
+	 * A restart only ever happens after the focus-loss debounce (30
+	 * frames on the new scene, AGC already re-converged) or an
+	 * explicit trigger, so the start skip only needs to cover the
+	 * jump back to position 0.
+	 */
+	context.configuration.focus.skip = kBigMoveSettleFrames;
+	context.configuration.focus.fine_pass = false;
+	context.configuration.focus.seed_baseline = false;
+	context.configuration.focus.last_was_max = false;
+	context.configuration.focus.sharp_prev = 0;
+	context.configuration.focus.sharp_before_max = 0;
+	context.configuration.focus.sharp_after_max = 0;
 	context.activeState.knobs.focus_pos = 0;
 	context.configuration.focus.lost_frames = 0;
 	context.activeState.knobs.focus_sweep = true;
@@ -139,13 +228,27 @@ void Af::restart(IPAContext &context) {
 }
 
 void Af::step(IPAContext &context, double& focus_pos, uint64_t sharp, bool& sweep){
+	auto &focus = context.configuration.focus;
 	steps ++;
-	// Even for sweep, we need some time to move to new lens position
-	if(context.configuration.focus.skip != 0){
-		context.configuration.focus.skip --;
+	/* Discard frames until the lens has settled at the commanded position. */
+	if(focus.skip != 0){
+		focus.skip --;
 		return;
 	}
 	if (!sweep) {
+		if (focus.seed_baseline) {
+			/*
+			 * First settled frame at the lock position: seed the
+			 * focus-loss baseline from what the lens actually
+			 * delivers here. The sweep maximum is unsuitable as
+			 * a baseline -- it is the largest of ~30 noisy
+			 * samples (biased high) and may include AGC drift.
+			 */
+			focus.sharpness_max = sharp;
+			focus.seed_baseline = false;
+			focus.lost_frames = 0;
+			return;
+		}
 		/*
 		 * Locked. Steady-state sharpness is noisy (AGC breathing,
 		 * hand shake), so nothing short of a deep, sustained drop
@@ -155,10 +258,10 @@ void Af::step(IPAContext &context, double& focus_pos, uint64_t sharp, bool& swee
 		 * noise/AGC spike made the locked position look permanently
 		 * "lost" and re-triggered full sweeps back to back.
 		 */
-		uint64_t &baseline = context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max;
+		uint64_t &baseline = focus.sharpness_max;
 		if (sharp * kFocusLostDen < baseline * kFocusLostNum) {
 			/* Deep drop: freeze the baseline and count. */
-			if (++context.configuration.focus.lost_frames >= kFocusLostFrames) {
+			if (++focus.lost_frames >= kFocusLostFrames) {
 				LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Info)
 					<< "Focus lost -- " << sharp << " vs "
 					<< baseline;
@@ -166,39 +269,94 @@ void Af::step(IPAContext &context, double& focus_pos, uint64_t sharp, bool& swee
 			}
 			return;
 		}
-		context.configuration.focus.lost_frames = 0;
+		focus.lost_frames = 0;
 		if (sharp > baseline)
 			baseline += (sharp - baseline) >> kBaselineRiseShift;
 		else
 			baseline -= (baseline - sharp) >> kBaselineDecayShift;
 		return;
 	}
-	if (sharp > context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max) {
-		context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max = sharp;
-		context.configuration.focus.focus_max_pos = focus_pos;
+
+	/*
+	 * Sweeping: score one settled frame at the current position,
+	 * remembering the samples on either side of the running maximum
+	 * for the parabolic refinement at the end of the fine pass.
+	 */
+	if (sharp > focus.sharpness_max) {
+		focus.sharpness_max = sharp;
+		focus.focus_max_pos = focus_pos;
+		focus.sharp_before_max = focus.sharp_prev;
+		focus.sharp_after_max = 0;
+		focus.last_was_max = true;
+	} else {
+		if (focus.last_was_max)
+			focus.sharp_after_max = sharp;
+		focus.last_was_max = false;
 	}
-	focus_pos += context.configuration.focus.step;	
-	if (focus_pos > context.configuration.focus.start && focus_pos < context.configuration.focus.stop)
+	focus.sharp_prev = sharp;
+
+	if (focus_pos + focus.step <= focus.stop + kPosEpsilon) {
+		focus_pos += focus.step;
+		focus.skip = kSettleFrames;
 		return;
+	}
 
-	int spread = 5;
-	context.configuration.focus.start = std::clamp(context.configuration.focus.focus_max_pos - context.configuration.focus.step*spread, 0.0, 100.0);
-	context.configuration.focus.stop = std::clamp(context.configuration.focus.focus_max_pos +  context.configuration.focus.step*spread, 0.0, 100.0);
-	LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Info) << "Best focus on step " <<context.configuration.focus.step << " (" << context.configuration.focus.start << ".." << context.configuration.focus.stop << "): " << focus_pos << " value " << context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max;
-	focus_pos = context.configuration.focus.start;
-	context.configuration.focus.step /= 10; // HERE
-	context.configuration.focus.skip = 10; // We need lens to settle after big move
-	if (context.configuration.focus.step > 0.2){
-		// We want to search for maximum at smaller step, forget maximum from prev step
-		context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max = 0;
+	if (!focus.fine_pass) {
+		/*
+		 * Coarse pass done: rescan +-kFineSpan around its peak
+		 * with kFineStep. Restart the maximum tracking -- the
+		 * fine samples are scored under (slightly) different AGC
+		 * than the coarse ones, so the two sets don't compare.
+		 */
+		LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Info)
+			<< "Coarse peak " << focus.focus_max_pos
+			<< " value " << focus.sharpness_max;
+		focus.fine_pass = true;
+		focus.start = std::clamp(focus.focus_max_pos - kFineSpan, 0.0, 100.0);
+		focus.stop = std::clamp(focus.focus_max_pos + kFineSpan, 0.0, 100.0);
+		focus.step = kFineStep;
+		focus.sharpness_max = 0;
+		focus.sharp_prev = 0;
+		focus.sharp_before_max = 0;
+		focus.sharp_after_max = 0;
+		focus.last_was_max = false;
+		focus_pos = focus.start;
+		focus.skip = kBigMoveSettleFrames;
 		return;
 	}
 
-	//We are done
+	/*
+	 * Fine pass done. Refine the peak by fitting a parabola through
+	 * the maximum and its two settled neighbours (uniform kFineStep
+	 * spacing): vertex = step/2 * (s- - s+) / (s- - 2*s0 + s+). Only
+	 * valid when both neighbours exist (maximum not at a window
+	 * edge) and the three points are strictly concave. The vertex of
+	 * a genuine local maximum lies within half a step of the sampled
+	 * maximum, so clamp there to bound the effect of noise.
+	 */
+	double lock_pos = focus.focus_max_pos;
+	if (focus.sharp_before_max != 0 && focus.sharp_after_max != 0) {
+		const double sm = static_cast<double>(focus.sharp_before_max);
+		const double s0 = static_cast<double>(focus.sharpness_max);
+		const double sp = static_cast<double>(focus.sharp_after_max);
+		const double denom = sm - 2.0 * s0 + sp;
+		if (denom < 0.0) {
+			double offset = 0.5 * (sm - sp) / denom * focus.step;
+			offset = std::clamp(offset, -focus.step / 2.0, focus.step / 2.0);
+			lock_pos = std::clamp(lock_pos + offset, 0.0, 100.0);
+		}
+	}
+
 	sweep = false;
-	LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Info) << "Sweep end. Best focus: " << context.configuration.focus.focus_max_pos << " steps " << steps;
-	// We want to keep context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max, to detect when scene changes (aka focus lost)
-	focus_pos = context.configuration.focus.focus_max_pos;
+	focus.focus_max_pos = lock_pos;
+	focus_pos = lock_pos;
+	/*
+	 * Settle at the lock position, then let the first settled frame
+	 * seed the focus-loss baseline (see the locked branch above).
+	 */
+	focus.skip = kBigMoveSettleFrames;
+	focus.seed_baseline = true;
+	LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Info) << "Sweep end. Best focus: " << lock_pos << " steps " << steps;
 }
 
 void Af::process([[maybe_unused]] IPAContext &context,
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/ipa_context.h b/src/ipa/simple/ipa_context.h
index cbe3b76..8deaaa0 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/ipa_context.h
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/ipa_context.h
@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@ struct IPASessionConfiguration {
 		double start, stop, step;
 		uint32_t skip;
 		uint32_t lost_frames;
+		/* CDAF sweep state (af.cpp) */
+		bool fine_pass;
+		bool seed_baseline;
+		bool last_was_max;
+		uint64_t sharp_prev;
+		uint64_t sharp_before_max;
+		uint64_t sharp_after_max;
 	} focus;
 };
 
